Fail a transaction older than a table's metadata, not the whole database.

A transaction reads an Iceberg table as the table was when the transaction
started, and finds that state in the table's metadata log. When the table's
latest metadata is newer than the transaction and no entry of the log is as
old (another connection created the table since, or changed it more times
since than the log keeps), the lookup threw an InternalException. DuckDB
invalidates its whole database on an InternalException thrown while a
statement runs, and a listing of the catalog (duckdb_tables(),
information_schema, pg_catalog) runs the lookup for every table any
connection has loaded. A pilot deployment went down this way: a transaction
block's INSERT had Igloo list the catalog's tables to check the user's
grants, the listing met a table another session had created and read since
the block began, and every session failed with "database has been
invalidated" until the process was restarted. The lookup now throws a
TransactionException, which fails only the transaction and asks the client
to restart it (Igloo answers SQLSTATE 40001, as for a conflicting commit),
and names the table. The start time it printed was milliseconds read as
microseconds, a date in 1970.

diff --git a/src/catalog/rest/catalog_entry/table/iceberg_table_information.cpp b/src/catalog/rest/catalog_entry/table/iceberg_table_information.cpp
index ebe8313..77412e7 100644
--- a/src/catalog/rest/catalog_entry/table/iceberg_table_information.cpp
+++ b/src/catalog/rest/catalog_entry/table/iceberg_table_information.cpp
@@ -634,9 +634,18 @@ IcebergTableMetadata IcebergTableInformation::CreateMetadataFromLog(ClientContex
 		}
 	}
 	if (!log_item_index.IsValid()) {
-		throw InternalException(
-		    "Metadata-log exists but none of the entries were valid for the current transaction start time (%s)",
-		    Timestamp::ToString(timestamp_ms_t(transaction_start_millis)));
+		//! Igloo: the table has no metadata from before the transaction started: another connection made
+		//! it since (and changed it once more, which put its first metadata in the log), or changed it more
+		//! times since than the log keeps. That is a concurrent session's doing, not a broken invariant:
+		//! DuckDB invalidates the whole database on an InternalException thrown while a statement runs (a
+		//! listing, which reads every table's entry, here), and every connection then failed until the
+		//! process restarted. The transaction cannot see the table as of its start; a new one can. The
+		//! start is milliseconds since the epoch, which the message printed as microseconds (1970).
+		throw TransactionException(
+		    "Table %s changed after this transaction started at %s UTC, and its metadata log keeps nothing "
+		    "from before then: it was created since, or changed more times since than the log keeps. Please "
+		    "restart your transaction",
+		    GetTableKey(), Timestamp::ToString(Timestamp::FromEpochMs(transaction_start_millis)));
 	}
 
 	auto fs = make_shared_ptr<CachingFileSystemWrapper>(FileSystem::GetFileSystem(context), *context.db);
